{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> The sense of <b>stiff-necked</b>: that he does not heed what was commanded — like a man walking on his way at a run, who does not turn his neck back to the one calling him. And this parable is because Israel were in the land of Egypt worshippers of idols, and HaShem sent prophets to them, saying: \"Each man, cast away the idols of Egypt,\" for thus it is written. And Moses recounted this deed to the children before his death, and he is the guardian of the senses, not the words. \"Go, get down, for your people has corrupted\" (Exodus 32:7), and it is written \"Arise, get down\" (Deuteronomy 9:12). And there it is written \"they bowed to it and said, 'These are your Elohim,'\" and it is written \"And now leave Me\" (Exodus 32:10), and corresponding to it \"Let Me be\" (Deuteronomy 9:14). And it is written \"My anger will burn against them and I will consume them\" (Exodus 32:10), and in place of this \"I will destroy them and blot out their name\" (Deuteronomy 9:14). And it is written \"I will make you into a great nation\" (Exodus 32:10), and \"mightier than it.\" And the senses are equal."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Resolved paragraph markers (פ' ז, פ' יוד) as Exodus chapter 32 verses 7 and 10 respectively. The phrase 'ועצום ממנו' is rendered as a truncated continuation of the Deuteronomy parallel; Ibn Ezra cites it without introducing verb or subject."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:46.425963240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}